  "body": "## What changed\n\nReplaces #96's turning-rapid exemption with a rapid check in the lathe's own cross-section (the meridian plane).\n\n- `operation/turning_rapids.rs`: for a turning op, every axial rapid (no XY travel) is judged in the meridian plane against the fitted spindle axis. Turning/Bore inserts sweep their nose disc (nose radius − GOUGE_TOL); groove, thread and form tools are judged at their tip, because a form tool's `nose_radius` is its crown. Material = part + setup stock revolved about the axis, minus this op's own earlier feeds (signed radius, so a facing pass across the axis counts), minus the stock faced off ahead (#89's prior read, revolved), minus any axial Drill ahead (a cylinder plus a cone point). A hit is `RapidInStock` and blocks the post. If the axis fit fails, the column law's verdict stands.\n- `operation/turning_outline.rs` (new): reads material per station as an annulus [r_in, r_out]. r_out comes from the turned outline; r_in comes from rays cast out from the axis. So a bored part or tube stock reads its hole as air, and a solid Cylinder stays solid to the axis.\n- `job.rs` collects the prior for turning ops too. The costly read only runs once a rapid is already convicted.\n- Fixtures: the lathe suites declared a 40 mm box stock around a 12 mm bar, and their approaches really were inside it. They now use a bar-sized Cylinder. No NC golden changed. `turning_bore` runs an axial pilot drill (`AX0`, which sorts ahead in name order, with a 70 mm-flute `DR-0400-L`) ahead of the bore.\n\n## Readings / pins\n\n- `turning_axial_rapids::an_axial_approach_inside_a_wider_bar_is_named_and_blocks_the_post`: fails on origin/main (`the approach into the bar went unnamed: []`) and passes here.\n- `turning_axial_rapids::the_same_approach_beside_a_bar_the_parts_size_is_clean`\n- `turning_bore::a_boring_approach_into_a_solid_bar_with_no_pilot_is_convicted_and_blocks_the_post`\n- Unit tests: meridian convictions, the annulus reading and the pilot cone.\n- Suites green (debug): lib, turning_bore 8, turning_axial_rapids 2, turning_contour 10, lathe_post 5 (goldens unchanged), drill_prior 10, drill_prior_kinds 4, turning / profile / blade / form / thread, lathe_field_sim, vertical_rapid_stock, posting, golden_cl. Clippy -p camcraft-app is clean.\n\n## Follow-ups\n\n- #130: turning kernels approach from the part, not the stock.\n- #109: a turning op's stamp doesn't digest the drill/facing ops ahead.\n- #127: rest.rs is over 400 lines.\n\nChangelog: A turned path's axial rapids are judged in the meridian plane against the revolved stock (the bore as air, a pilot drill ahead credited); one into the bar blocks the post\n\nFixes #103\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
